{
  "name": "Heart of Fire",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Whenever you hit a creature with a spell of 1st level or higher that deals fire damage or it fails a save against such a spell, you also set it aflame.</p><p>A creature that is aflame takes fire damage equal to twice your Proficiency at the start of each of its turns and sheds bright light in a radius of 10 feet and dim light light in a radius of 10 feet beyond that for 1 minute.</p><p>At the end of each of its turns, an affected creature can make a DEX Saving Throw against your spell save DC to end the effect on itself. Alternatively, it or another creature can spend an Action to put out the flames.</p>",
